<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cree</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cree people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cree are one of the largest Indigenous peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, speaking Algonquian languages, with lands stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a> lowlands to the northern plains. They were key partners of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a>, and the Plains Cree joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assiniboine">Assiniboine</a> in the Iron Confederacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cree.jpg" alt="Cree" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Noahedits · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cree_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
